# Lane workflow v2

This applies to every agent working a PropLane lane (Cursor and Codex alike),
for Prakrit's process. Full contract: `docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md`.

1. **Sync first.** When the tree is clean: `git fetch origin && git merge
   --no-edit origin/prakrit` (and `origin/main` too if `prakrit` is behind it).
   Do this at the start of every prompt, before anything else.
2. **Plan in the studio first.** Write or update this lane's plan in the
   PropLane studio (`~/proplane-mock-kit`, `node tools/studio-plan.mjs new
   --lane <lane> --id <id> --title "<title>"`) before touching product code.
   Skip only when the captain literally says **"skip plan"**.
3. **Build only once the plan is buildable** — check with
   `node ~/proplane-mock-kit/tools/studio-plan.mjs status --lane <branch>`
   (exits 0 when the status is `approved`, `built`, or `skipped`).
4. **Run the test gate after building**: `npm run gate:prompt`.
5. **Never push a protected branch** (`prakrit`, `main`, `staging`,
   `production`). Code reaches `prakrit` only when the captain types
   `/promote prakrit` in the lane's own pane; local hooks enforce the
   `prakrit` lock and refuse a push to any protected branch outside that flow.
   Push only your own lane, fast-forward only.
